---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, DEFAULT_QUOTA, SIGNUP_CURL, SITE_TITLE, WHAT_YOU_GET, X_HANDLE, X_URL } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Pricing — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Everything on nano-api is free while the service is young. No card, no trial clock, no feature held back."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="page">
				<p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
				<h1>Free, for now. All of it.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Every service, every feature, no card. Signup is one call and the key comes back in the
					response.
				</p>
				<pre class="signup"><code>{SIGNUP_CURL}</code></pre>

				<div class="card offer">
					<p class="price">$0</p>
					<p class="quota">
						{DEFAULT_QUOTA} monitors or schedules to start — ask for more, still free
					</p>
					<ul>
						{WHAT_YOU_GET.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
					</ul>
					<a class="button" href="/howto/#setup">Start in curl</a>
				</div>

				<h2>Why free</h2>
				<p>
					One person, alongside a day job. Charging makes promises about response times and uptime
					I am not ready to make. The infrastructure costs a few dollars a month whether you use it
					or not.
				</p>

				<h2>When that changes</h2>
				<ul class="promises">
					<li>Notice by email, well before anything costs money.</li>
					<li>Nothing switched off without you agreeing first.</li>
					<li>Nothing you built breaks; the API does not change shape because billing does.</li>
					<li>Anyone using it before then keeps a free allowance.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Limits that exist anyway</h2>
				<p>Technical, not commercial — they stop one account taking the service down for everyone.</p>
				<ul class="promises">
					<li>{DEFAULT_QUOTA} monitors or schedules by default. Ask, and it goes up.</li>
					<li>Ping payloads 2 KB; scheduled request bodies 8 KB.</li>
					<li>Scheduled calls: 60s timeout, 3 attempts, public HTTPS targets only.</li>
					<li>100 distinct lock names, lease up to an hour.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Questions you would reasonably ask</h2>

				<div class="qa">
					<h3>How do I get a key?</h3>
					<p>
						<code>POST /v1/signup</code> with an email address. No verification mail: the key is the
						credential and the address is a label, so a click would add a mail provider and stop
						nobody. Three per address per hour keeps it honest. Questions still go to
						<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or
						<a href={X_URL} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{X_HANDLE}</a> on X.
					</p>

					<h3>What happens at the limit?</h3>
					<p>
						Creating the next one is refused. Pings and runs for things that already exist are
						<strong>never</strong> refused for quota reasons.
					</p>

					<h3>How fast will I know?</h3>
					<p>
						A sweep runs every minute, so alerts land within about a minute of the deadline. Need
						second-level precision? Say so — that is a different product.
					</p>

					<h3>Where do alerts go?</h3>
					<p>
						Any HTTPS webhook. The body is Slack-shaped (<code>text</code> at the top level), so a
						Slack webhook needs no configuration. Email and SMS are not built.
					</p>

					<h3>Is there a dashboard?</h3>
					<p>
						No — only an API, on purpose. The <a href="/howto/">how-to page</a> is the whole
						product in curl.
					</p>

					<h3>What if the service itself goes down?</h3>
					<p>
						Then you are not monitored. No SLA while it is free, and I will not promise one I
						cannot keep. Where a missed alert matters, run two providers.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="closing card">
					<h2>Start now, pay nothing</h2>
					<p>{DEFAULT_QUOTA} things watched or run, upgradeable by asking.</p>
					<a class="button" href="/howto/#setup">Start in curl</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.page {
		max-width: 46em;
		padding: 2em 0 0;
	}
	.lede {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}
	.signup {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		margin: 1em 0 0;
	}
	.offer {
		margin: 2em 0 1em;
		border-color: var(--alive-dim);
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--alive-dim), var(--box-shadow);
	}
	.price {
		font-size: 3rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin: 0;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
	}
	.quota {
		font-family: var(--mono);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--alive);
		margin: 0.2em 0 1.2em;
	}
	.offer ul {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0 0 1.6em;
		padding: 1.2em 0 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		gap: 0.5em 1.4em;
		font-size: 0.93rem;
	}
	.offer li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1.5em;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.offer li::before {
		content: "✓";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--alive);
	}
	h2 {
		margin-top: 2.4em;
		font-size: 1.5rem;
	}
	.page p {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	ul.promises {
		padding-left: 1.2em;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	ul.promises li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.qa h3 {
		margin-top: 1.8em;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--text);
	}
	.closing {
		margin-top: 3em;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.closing h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.closing p {
		margin-bottom: 1.4em;
	}
	@media (max-width: 620px) {
		.offer ul {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
